hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1058","It is narrated on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Hafs, meaning Ibn Ghayath, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after greeting and speaking.”"
"1059","Abu Hashim Ziyad bin Ayyub and Yusuf bin Musa told us, they said: Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after speaking.” Abu Bakr said: If he meant Ibn Masoud By his saying after the speech, his saying when he prayed the noon prayer five times, and he said: Add more to the prayer, and he said: What is that? These words are from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello to the meaning of his words in the story of Dhul-Yadin, and if he meant the words that are in the other report when he prayed, whether it was more or less, then it was told to him, and he said: “I am only a human being. I forget just as you forget.” This is a word that the narrators differed about at the time the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke about it. As for Al-A’mash, in his narration, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, and Abu Bakr Al-Nahshali, in his narration, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, mentioned that these words were from him before the two prostrations of forgetfulness, and as for Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir, And Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah, they both mentioned in their reports on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah that these words came from him after He finished the two prostrations of forgetfulness, and it was not proven by uncontested news that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke while he knew and remembered that he had to You prostrated by forgetfulness, and it has been proven that he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, spoke forgetfully after greeting him, and he did not know that he had done it by mistake, which he must do. He prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then he performed the two prostrations of forgetfulness after he had spoken, forgetfully"
